From 1ee88989f34e09a76c7a87f97c4afc59e43fd053 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tsetsen-erdene Ganbaatar <dis446@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:31:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): harden /new against rejected clears and stale state

Wait for the Clear Done (and its SessionId) before resetting the remote view or sending RenameSession, so a rejected clear leaves the old transcript intact and never renames the old session. Correlate the clear with its request id, drop the pending operation on disconnect, and consume the Done as a control acknowledgement.

Clear active skill, improve mode, and provider session state in the remote reset, refresh the terminal title and /resume cache for every local reset, and suppress the duplicate rename notice that /new used to print through the normal SessionRenamed path. RenameSession now returns its request id for correlation.

Cover the deferred ack, Clear rejection, stale state, quiet rename, and /clear working-directory behavior.
